# data_shadows.syms — external DATA-constant symbols forced to header-less
# OBJECT shadows by abigen (--data-shadow-file). These are NSString*/CF
# object constants exported by NATIVE x86_64 frameworks (an app's bundled
# PRIVATE frameworks like RedRock/iLifeSlideshow, plus a few ObjC system
# frameworks not in ABICONV_SYM_SOURCES). A translated i386 binary reads them
# `movl slot,%reg; movl (%reg),%reg`, which truncates the real >4GB symbol
# address and faults. Header-typed NS*/CF* constants get shadows via the
# consider set; these have no headers, so they are listed explicitly. The
# shadow is a low-4GB var holding an objc handle wrapping the real object
# (x64_init_data_shadows + dlsym); static-interpose redirects the bind to it.
#
# GENERIC: regenerate/extend for any app with
#   src/86x64/_extract_data_shadows.sh <app.dylib> <libabiconv.dylib>
# and union the output here. dlsym-miss is a no-op, so unrelated apps that
# don't import a symbol are unaffected. Seeded from iPhoto (iLife '11).
